{"title":"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Titu Andreescu, Gabriel Dospinescu</i>) For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> a positive integer, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096c6f57e7b24a794f4dae227e6f3f0cf7ed9c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> be the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39abfe232e2ed5247aa4028089e5f651090e66da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the minimal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> for which there  exists a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers such that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be1501b495383c6962007bcc1e90c79166e8b4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\left(\\sum_{x\\in X} x\\right) = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"115\" height=\"53\" /> for any nonempty subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f99ddd921a4de2d03b86d503d3a115d38b5f5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X\\subset S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.  Prove that there are constants <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9deb8c960d5bdfb341bb7cd58b5a9eba3a8e75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; C_1 &lt; C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" /> with\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/7/73781eed2cabf9a48a7d376ce6846b3fb2b631f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[C_1 \\log_{10} n \\le f(n) \\le C_2 \\log_{10} n.\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For the upper bound, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the smallest integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5fabda30e9180a16dfa848ca1565687082884c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^p\\geq n(n+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" /> and let\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f24256c0a9d61d7cb560834de4cf1d08206c150.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S = \\{10^p - 1, 2(10^p - 1), \\ldots, n(10^p - 1)\\}.\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"18\" />\nThe sum of any nonempty set of elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> will have the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/c/45cba2ad4a621458ce88c3a93843c6e53d3563ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(10^p - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faffe6fc89aeff052ee05a61e990c4bee31282e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq k\\leq n(n+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />. Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/9/e69722d0d85526d6ebbb1d1760f64728733f0b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(10^p - 1) = [(k - 1)10^p] + [(10^p - 1) - (k - 1)]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"376\" height=\"18\" />. The second term gives the bottom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> digits of the sum and the first term gives at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> top digits. Since the sum of a digit of the second term and the corresponding digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/c/efce61aab04f52f5d37708f357df021c8baa7434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> is always 9, the sum of the digits will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfccc41c5aaf4c5d594b22144b38bab60ee1c9fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb15018c1c3b8ffb14a00a61dca8818ec1b8177.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{p-1} &lt; n(n+1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"19\" />, this example shows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e515b030fac80ab38df779b536a48496eee95bbf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)\\leq 9p\\leq 9\\log_{10}(5n(n+1)).\\]\" width=\"245\" height=\"18\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c1ca449ad9f874c1c7cefb996333eeb9aeebe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5(n + 1) &lt; n^4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"21\" />, and hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/2/482232075c780231484c5618a803a24733786246.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n) &lt; 9\\log_{10}n^5 = 45\\log_{10}n.\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"19\" />\nFor the lower bound, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47affecc93688552c8eca8bc13560d52b4cc28a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> positive integers such that any nonempty <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f99ddd921a4de2d03b86d503d3a115d38b5f5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X\\subset S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40b3c1976a029894c465e5a0daee41a93e5acc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\left(\\sum_{x\\in X} x\\right) = f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"140\" height=\"53\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096c6f57e7b24a794f4dae227e6f3f0cf7ed9c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> is always congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> modulo 9, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/1675e7319351835d865b52300d9798f99010f1f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{x\\in X} x\\equiv f(n)\\pmod{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"172\" height=\"39\" /> for all nonempty <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f99ddd921a4de2d03b86d503d3a115d38b5f5c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X\\subset S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. Hence every element of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> must be a multiple of 9 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d2aff1d39b2b007cb685f103087acaa4eb48d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)\\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the largest positive integer such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813aa706473d5ef7efdbe9f18bbb2d63dc6cef52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^q - 1\\leq n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />. Lemma 1 below shows that there is a nonempty subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/f/1bfe5c36718cfff3047aeb5a00c7875ea2fcc6c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{x\\in X} x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"41\" height=\"39\" /> a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40175c521426d109925966cca57ceb937c433e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^q - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, and hence Lemma 2 shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b1261c2dc41892f2c0d8f4ca6d97f9d075c11762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)\\geq 9q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Lemma 1.</b> Any set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers contains a nonempty subset whose sum is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i> Suppose a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has no nonempty subset with sum divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. Look at the possible sums mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> of nonempty subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. Adding a new element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will give at least one new sum mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, namely the least multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> which does not already occur. Therefore the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> has at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/7/fc73f3216cbfb7ceb707c9c143823d7e5e49f659.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> distinct sums mod <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> of nonempty subsets and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/6/3d62be16e463ff3098916dbac95f78c434f07670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|T| &lt; m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><b>Lemma 2.</b> Any positive multiple <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40175c521426d109925966cca57ceb937c433e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^q - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ec2f3411bbc3445e84a01fcfd86cb5af92714ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(M)\\geq 9q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i> Suppose on the contrary that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest positive multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40175c521426d109925966cca57ceb937c433e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^q - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/5/9651a55341a0d223aabd62ab15c77c5b84e19a92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(M) &lt; 9q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874507d6e30fccddbc1da6508b1bbcaf0b291837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M\\neq 10^q - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />, hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010137195166ca64abd4496b02776b1ddfa4dc5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M &gt; 10^q$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"68\" height=\"13\" />. Suppose the most significant digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e0b9717c792b0048e311636fcf285bf0d18bfae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^m$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"29\" height=\"13\" /> digit, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/7646b82d87e2a35b557fcfe46c92010e9aaab003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\geq q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d57f420b0128451268ceedd4e8f555716894191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = M - 10^{m-q}(10^q - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"199\" height=\"18\" /> is a smaller positive multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40175c521426d109925966cca57ceb937c433e9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^q - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> and has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953be58c9a15455f0f2eaee33f2d35bb910c5f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s(N)\\leq s(M) &lt; 9q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, a contradiction. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Finally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008ed6fcd75f9bd0ff41b7e364404d1223337b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{q+1} &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/3/ae36ee9298dd4387d382285949e5da3d8292ced4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q + 1 &gt; \\log_{10} n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"19\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b1261c2dc41892f2c0d8f4ca6d97f9d075c11762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)\\geq 9q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d2aff1d39b2b007cb685f103087acaa4eb48d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)\\geq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3bfe0b557f057063d3e15272a4ff0aadf08927e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)\\geq \\frac{9q + 9}{2} &gt; \\frac{9}{2}\\log_{10}n.\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"37\" />\nWeaker versions of Lemmas 1 and 2 are still sufficient to prove the desired type of lower bound.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n-mahthir marshad\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO\" title=\"2005 USAMO\">2005 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205933\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.043 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.069 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 447/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1633/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 55/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14379/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.017      1 -total\n 37.37%    6.359      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 31.